@startuml workspaces
title Workspaces: membership, invitations and ownership
autonumber
actor "User" as User
participant "CLI / TUI\nPresentation" as Client
participant "CLI internal/app" as ClientApp
participant "Document client\nHTTP OR gRPC adapter" as Remote
box "hermes-document-service" #E0F4E0
participant "API + session middleware" as API
participant "internal/app" as App
participant "internal/domain\nPolicies / invariants" as Domain
participant "internal/postgres\nUnitOfWork / repositories" as Repo
end box
database "Document PostgreSQL" as DB
note over Remote, App
  Protected requests follow auth.puml: middleware -> Auth -> Redis SessionStore.
  Only a valid session reaches the use case; Redis failure returns unavailable.
  App receives authenticated identity, never a client-supplied actor ID.
  Domain access checks use current data through repositories.
end note
note over App, DB
  Mutations use one PostgreSQL transaction with current access and version checks.
  Any failed check rolls back all writes; unchanged state creates no change event.
  Domain facts from committed changes follow events_dispatch.puml.
  Outbox/CDC versus direct publication remains OPEN (ADR-002).
end note

== Create shared workspace ==
User -> Client : CreateWorkspace(name, description)
Client -> ClientApp : Workspaces.Create
ClientApp -> Remote : CreateWorkspace
Remote -> API : Protected request
API -> App : Workspaces.Create(actor, request)
App -> Repo : WithinTransaction; load active actor
Repo -> DB : BEGIN; SELECT active user
App -> Domain : Validate workspace + owner membership
App -> Repo : Create shared workspace and owner membership
Repo -> DB : INSERT; COMMIT or ROLLBACK
App --> API : Workspace/version + committed WorkspaceCreated/MemberAdded facts / error
API --> Remote : Result
Remote --> ClientApp : Result
ClientApp --> Client : Result

== List, read and select ==
ClientApp -> Remote : ListWorkspaces(cursor) / GetWorkspace(id)
Remote -> API : Protected query
API -> App : Workspaces.List / Get(actor, query)
App -> Repo : Query active workspaces by current membership
Repo -> DB : Access-filtered SELECT; personal workspace included
Repo --> App : Page / workspace / unavailable
App --> API : Result; no change events
API --> Remote : Result
Remote --> ClientApp : Result
ClientApp -> ClientApp : ConfigStore saves selected workspace only on success
note over ClientApp, App
  Selection is local context and grants no access.
  Subsequent operations recheck current membership.
end note

== Update name or description ==
ClientApp -> Remote : UpdateWorkspace(id, changes, expected_version)
Remote -> API : Protected request
API -> App : Workspaces.Update(actor, request)
App -> Repo : Transaction: load active workspace, membership and version
Repo -> DB : BEGIN; read current state
App -> Domain : Require owner/admin; personal workspace requires owner; check version
App -> Repo : Persist actual changes with new version, or no-op / rollback
Repo -> DB : UPDATE and COMMIT / no-op / ROLLBACK
App --> API : Result; WorkspaceUpdated only for committed changes
API --> Remote : Result
Remote --> ClientApp : Result

== Invite existing user ==
ClientApp -> Remote : InviteMember(workspace, invitee, role)
Remote -> API : Protected request
API -> App : Workspaces.InviteMember(actor, request)
App -> Repo : Transaction: load workspace, actor role, active invitee and pending invitations
Repo -> DB : BEGIN; SELECT current state
App -> Domain : Shared workspace; owner may invite admin/editor/viewer;\nadmin may invite editor/viewer; reject member/duplicate pending invitation
App -> Repo : Create expiring invitation if valid
Repo -> DB : INSERT; enforce constraints; COMMIT / ROLLBACK
App --> API : Invitation + WorkspaceInvitationCreated fact / error
API --> Remote : Result
Remote --> ClientApp : Result

== Respond to invitation ==
User -> Client : Accept / decline invitation
Client -> ClientApp : Workspaces.RespondToInvitation
ClientApp -> Remote : RespondToInvitation(id, decision)
Remote -> API : Protected request
API -> App : Workspaces.RespondToInvitation(actor, request)
App -> Repo : Transaction: lock invitation; load active workspace/recipient
Repo -> DB : BEGIN; SELECT current invitation
App -> Domain : Require addressed user, pending status and unexpired invitation
alt Accept valid invitation
  App -> Repo : Create membership; mark accepted
else Decline valid invitation
  App -> Repo : Mark declined
else Invalid, expired or concurrently changed
  App -> Repo : Roll back; return error
end
Repo -> DB : COMMIT accepted changes / ROLLBACK
App --> API : Result; Accepted + MemberAdded / Declined facts after commit
API --> Remote : Result
Remote --> ClientApp : Result

== Revoke or expire invitation ==
ClientApp -> Remote : RevokeInvitation(id)
Remote -> API : Protected request
API -> App : Workspaces.RevokeInvitation(actor, id)
App -> Repo : Transaction: check management rights; serialize pending -> revoked
Repo -> DB : Conditional transition; COMMIT / ROLLBACK
App --> API : Result; WorkspaceInvitationRevoked only for actual transition
API --> Remote : Result
Remote --> ClientApp : Result
note over App, DB
  Expiration uses the same application/domain/repository boundary.
  Expired invitations cannot be accepted even before cleanup runs.
  Expiry scheduling is OPEN; do not assume a chosen background worker.
  Acceptance, revocation and expiration serialize on the invitation state.
end note

== Change role, remove member or leave ==
ClientApp -> Remote : ChangeRole / RemoveMember / LeaveWorkspace
Remote -> API : Protected request
API -> App : Workspaces membership use case(actor, request)
App -> Repo : Transaction: load workspace + affected memberships
Repo -> DB : BEGIN; read/lock current state
App -> Domain : Reject personal workspace; protect owner; only owner manages admins;\nadmin cannot change owner/admin membership; check requested role
App -> Repo : Apply membership change and remove inaccessible subscriptions
Repo -> DB : COMMIT valid changes / ROLLBACK
App --> API : Result; MemberRoleChanged / MemberRemoved facts for actual changes
API --> Remote : Result
Remote --> ClientApp : Result

== Transfer ownership ==
ClientApp -> Remote : TransferOwnership(id, new_owner, expected_version)
Remote -> API : Protected request
API -> App : Workspaces.TransferOwnership(actor, request)
App -> Repo : Transaction: serialize workspace and affected users/memberships
Repo -> DB : BEGIN; read/lock current state
App -> Domain : Current owner only; shared workspace; active new member; matching version
App -> Repo : Update owner_id; new member -> owner; previous owner -> admin; increment version
Repo -> DB : COMMIT all changes / ROLLBACK
App --> API : Result; WorkspaceOwnershipTransferred after commit
API --> Remote : Result
Remote --> ClientApp : Result

== Delete shared workspace ==
User -> Client : Confirm deletion after reviewing consequences
Client -> ClientApp : Workspaces.Delete(id, expected_version, confirmation)
ClientApp -> Remote : DeleteWorkspace
Remote -> API : Protected request
API -> App : Workspaces.Delete(actor, request)
App -> Repo : Transaction: load/lock workspace and current membership
Repo -> DB : BEGIN
App -> Domain : Require owner, shared kind, matching version and confirmation
App -> Repo : Capture former members; soft-delete workspace; close documents/memberships;\nrevoke invitations and remove subscriptions
Repo -> DB : COMMIT all changes / ROLLBACK
App --> API : Result; WorkspaceDeleted + changed invitation facts after commit
API --> Remote : Result
Remote --> ClientApp : Result
ClientApp -> ClientApp : Clear local selection on confirmed deletion only
note over App, DB
  Removal/deletion can produce a minimal notice for former members.
  It grants no access to documents; routing/eligibility is OPEN (events_dispatch.puml).
end note
@enduml
